          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            What is called
            %em Einstein-Yang-Mills-Dirac theory
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/physics"} physics
            is the
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/theory+%28physics%29"} theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+%28in+theoretical+physics%29"} model (in theoretical physics)
            describing
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gravity"} gravity
            together with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yang-Mills+fields"} Yang-Mills fields
            and coupled to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fermion"} fermionic
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/matter"} matter
          %p
            Einstein-Yang-Mills-Dirac theory is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+Lagrangian"} local Lagrangian
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+%28physics%29"} field
            theory defined by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+functional"} action functional
            which is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Einstein-Hilbert+action"} Einstein-Hilbert action
            plus the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yang-Mills+action+functional"} Yang-Mills action functional
            involving the given metric,
          .maruku-equation
